  "schema": "canli.alphac-drawdown-live-estimator.v1",
  "the_finding": "THE HALFLIFE IS THE LEVER AND THE WINDOW IS NOT. Shortening the halflife inside the production 720-bar window improves expected maximum drawdown monotonically: 10.25% at 720, 9.45% at 63, 8.38% at 21, 7.96% at 7. Shortening the WINDOW buys nothing on top of it \u2014 168/21 gives 8.52% against 720/21's 8.38%, inside the standard error. This corrects a claim published earlier the same day that named the window as the only lever; that came from sampling only halflives at or above 21 days, where the window truncates everything into one narrow band.",
