  "why_the_original_sweep_does_not_transfer": "analyze_frontier_14.py updates covariance with an UNTRUNCATED recursion \u2014 infinite memory, no window, no seed block. Production's ewma_cov is windowed at cov_window_bars and seeded with an equally weighted block of the oldest cov_min_periods rows, so the window BOUNDS the memory and a halflife longer than the window cannot be delivered. A halflife sweep on an untruncated estimator answers a question about a system this book does not run."
